= SMART

== Skill 1: Confident and Accurate Project Communication

*Specific*

I will improve my confidence and information recall skills by maintaining a detailed project information log. This log will summarize key facts about the topic alongside current findings and limitations for our project. This information log may or may not live within the project README itself. 

*Measurable*

As previously stated, this log will track facts, findings and limitations. These can be counted directly and verified for accuracy. The information contained in here should grow through the life cycle of the project.

I should also be studying this document regularly, so before any meeting with a client or professor I should be able to explain the project goal, data basics and a recent result without referring to this log. I will track instances where I slip up and either forget or misrepresent information to others. 

*Achievable*

This task doesn't need to be too time intensive. 15-30 minutes every couple days should be sufficient to both add to and update the log. As such this goal shouldn't dominate my time or cause me to prioritize it over other responsibilities. 

*Relevant*

This skill is extremely relevant. It allows for more seamless and accurate project communication while also enhancing my ability to interpret results. It may even help come up with solutions to problems we run into. 

*Time-bound*

I will have a skeleton of this log created within a week of getting access to the data. I will update this log twice per week during the semester. We can check in on this project log midway through the semester and discuss if it aided in my lack of confidence and recall. 

